## reading of the result, stated so the numbers are not misread
  Every file on both targets is outcome ok, lo ok and lo_in ok: all 27
  real workbooks opened in LibreOffice as input and as copy, on host and
  on i686.
  Every entry row on both targets is status identical: 870 per label,
  1740 in all, with recompressed, changed, dropped and added all 0. No
  entry content differs.
  diff_exit is 1 for all 54 rows, which xlsx-diff documents as
  "differences found", not an error; rows are trusted at exit 0 or 1.
  files_identical is no for all 54 rows, and flagged is non-zero, because
  of zip metadata only: attrs on all 870 entries, extra on 578, and
  gpflags, descriptor and local on 292 each; mtime and comment are 0.
  That is the spec P4 expectation, "every entry identical with the
  writer's flags catalogued", and not a fidelity defect.
  WORDING, a finding about the record and not about the run: the record
  section headed "Files not ok, with a diff exit other than 0, with a
  leftover temporary file, or failing the LibreOffice open check" lists
  all 54 rows. None of them is an open-check failure; every lo and lo_in
  in that table reads ok. They are listed on the diff_exit condition of a
  four-condition heading. The heading behaves as planning ruled, but a
  reader skimming it can take 54 rows for 54 failures.

